<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jakob Hannibal I of Hohenems</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1530–1587</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jakob <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a> I (1530–1587) was Count of Hohenems and a general in Spanish and papal service. A nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-iv">Pope Pius IV</a>, he fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>'s wars in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> and married Ortensia Borromeo, sister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-borromeo">Charles Borromeo</a>. With his brother Cardinal Mark Sittich he raised the family of Ems to wealth and the rank of imperial counts.</p></div>
